&lt;p&gt;A few years into RevOps, most people end up choosing between staying close to admin and reporting, or moving towards building automations and the AI tools that now sit on top of the CRM. The second path is hard to get onto if you haven&#39;t done it somewhere first.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this job you&#39;d do both, in a commercial team that already works with AI day to day through assistants connected to Salesforce, support tickets and product data, while marketing is being rebuilt the same way. You&#39;d build on that, starting next to the person who set most of it up and taking over the technical side from them. You&#39;d also keep the CRM and the data underneath it in good order. That&#39;s a lot of upkeep, like permissions, data cleanup and renewal notices to thousands of customers, and there&#39;s no ops team to share it with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airtame makes wireless screen-sharing devices and the cloud software that manages them, used in schools and workplaces around the world. Most of our volume goes through distributors on several continents, sometimes to customers our own reps sent them. Our sales team also works deals directly, and smaller orders come through our Shopify store. Running all three through one Salesforce makes for a harder data model than most RevOps roles come with.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re around 55 people, headquartered in Copenhagen, and we&#39;d prefer you to work from the office there. Remote from elsewhere in the EU works too. You&#39;d report to our Director of Customer Experience &amp;amp; Revenue Operations, who sets the roadmap with you and owns the metric definitions, and you&#39;d work with sales, customer experience, marketing and product every week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What Success Looks Like (Year 1)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the Commercial Stack&lt;/strong&gt;: By the end of the year the technical side has moved over to you, including the AI tools the team uses. You bring the roadmap to your manager and build it, and when sales or support want a system changed, you decide how it&#39;s done.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Send the Right Renewal Message&lt;/strong&gt;: Thousands of customers receive renewal notices. We&#39;re starting to ask customers in our cloud software how they intend to renew, and you&#39;d build the email flows that act on it, with a separate path for each way of renewing. If a notice doesn&#39;t go out, you know within hours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the Numbers Agree&lt;/strong&gt;: Pipeline, bookings, ARR, renewals and churn come out the same in every dashboard and every AI assistant, whether the sale came through Shopify, a rep or a distributor. Your manager sets the definitions, and you make sure every system uses them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate the Manual Work&lt;/strong&gt;: Find the processes worth automating and keep shipping them, tested in a sandbox first with a way back if something goes wrong. The first one is turning the pricing claims our distributors send, in all sorts of formats, into line-item pricing in Salesforce with an audit trail. As AI assistants get better at connecting to things on their own, part of this is also deciding what&#39;s still worth building ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bring Support onto Intercom&lt;/strong&gt;: We&#39;re moving customer support from Zendesk to Intercom. Depending on when you join, you&#39;d help finish the move or pick it up just after go-live, then own Intercom, including its Salesforce sync and the AI setup that gets customer feedback to the product team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You know Salesforce from the inside&lt;/strong&gt;. A few years of hands-on admin, including Flow Builder, permissions and the data model. You write SQL and SOQL and can model data for a report yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You ask why before you build&lt;/strong&gt;. You can tell us about a request you pushed back on, or a process you changed or dropped instead of automating it as asked, and what it was for in the first place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You work with AI by default&lt;/strong&gt;. You use AI tools every day to write flows and queries, and you keep up with what&#39;s new on your own. When a new connector makes something we built unnecessary, you&#39;re happy to retire it. If you&#39;ve connected tools through their APIs or written some Python or JavaScript, that&#39;s a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ve run a commercial system on your own&lt;/strong&gt;. At some point you&#39;ve been the only or main admin of a Salesforce org or a similar system, and you left documentation behind that someone else could take over from. Here there&#39;s no ops team behind you, so a broken sync in the morning and a dashboard request in the afternoon are both yours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Why Airtame?&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building on Top of Admin: You&#39;d keep the CRM running and build automations and AI tooling on top of it, starting next to the person who set most of it up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Most RevOps roles are purely SaaS or purely e-commerce. Here, you get to solve the unique intellectual challenge of bridging a hardware supply chain with a high-velocity digital subscription model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A healthy work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five weeks paid vacation and 5 days of extra paid AirtameFlex days.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension and private health insurance (on FTE Copenhagen contract).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible work environment, with a hybrid mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Catered lunch in the office.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Airtame is an equal opportunity employer. We have colleagues across the globe, with both in-office and full-time remote workers. This feeds into our international hybrid mindset, with people from 25+ nationalities that make up the Airtame team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work-life cultural balance is key to our success. Our team encompasses our values of trust and open communication to support each other and to collaborate in a fun and collective way.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we handle your application data&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Airtame ApS (CVR 35478973, Copenhagen), together with Airtame US Inc. for US roles, processes the information you submit to assess your application. We do this under the EU General Data Protection Regulation, wherever you are based. Your data is stored in Greenhouse, our recruiting system, which may store it outside the EU under standard EU safeguards. Only the people involved in hiring can see it. For roles with privileged access to our systems, we’ll contact one professional reference or previous employer that you name, to confirm your role and dates. We’ll tell you before we do. We keep your data for 6 months after the recruitment process ends, or longer where US law requires it or where you consent to us keeping it for future roles. To get a copy of your data, correct or delete it, or object to how we use it, write to &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:data@airtame.com&quot;&gt;data@airtame.com&lt;/a&gt;. You can also complain to the Danish Data Protection Agency (Datatilsynet).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;From the outside, video conferencing looks solved. Anyone who&#39;s worked on it knows better. At a big company, that work gets split a hundred ways, and you&#39;d own a slice of it. At a company our size, it&#39;s one person&#39;s call, and it would be yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re around 55 people, headquartered in Copenhagen, and you&#39;d work from there or remotely from within the EU. We build the hardware and the software that runs on it, so the conferencing you&#39;d work on runs on the device in the meeting room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Year one outcomes&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Put the telemetry in&lt;/strong&gt;. Conferencing quality is hard to see without the right instrumentation, so you&#39;d build it: latency, quality, and resource use on the device, visible and tracked. Once it&#39;s there, a bad call comes with the data to explain it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Move the metrics&lt;/strong&gt;. Better audio and video, lower latency, lighter load on the device. Agree on the handful that matter most, and show clear movement within the year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take on the problems that need a specialist&lt;/strong&gt;. Some conferencing issues need someone who&#39;s solved them before. You&#39;d own those from diagnosis to fix, and the recurring ones stop recurring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raise the team&#39;s game&lt;/strong&gt;. Share what you know so the team&#39;s calls on real-time media get sharper, and flag the wrong turns before they cost months. The bar you set becomes the team&#39;s default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ve lived in real-time media&lt;/strong&gt;. Years of it: WebRTC, codecs, the media server and its tricks, why a call holds together on one network and falls apart on another. You know the caveats because you&#39;ve hit them. And the brand names sit on the same ideas underneath, so where you learned it matters less to us than that you did.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You reach for data&lt;/strong&gt;. When something&#39;s off, you measure before you theorise. You&#39;ve built or leaned on telemetry to find what&#39;s going on in a messy real-time system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You lift the people around you&lt;/strong&gt;. You do it without needing a manager&#39;s title. You flag the caveat before someone hits it, steer a design away from a wrong turn, and people trust your read on a hard call.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You use AI as a daily tool.&lt;/strong&gt; You write code with it, debug with it, prototype with it. You&#39;ve formed your own view on where it speeds things up and where it gets in the way, and you help the people around you do the same.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Logistics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Location: Remote in Europe, or hybrid from our Copenhagen office.&lt;/p&gt;
